# Long-term goals (do not implement until asked)

These are roadmap constraints. Do **not** add crates, bindings, or Augusta modules for them until the user explicitly starts that work.

## Very long term — native bindings

Lovelace should eventually be able to generate / host bindings for:

- **SQLite**
- **raylib**
- **SDL**
- **GTK+** (maybe)
- A **native GUI** library (first-party Lovelace/Augusta GUI, not only wrapping GTK)

HOW TOs for writing bindings belong under `docs/` once that feature exists.

## Long term — Augusta native vs WASI 0.3

Augusta **native** must eventually expose **at least** the same capabilities WASI 0.3 provides to the **wasi** flavor (clocks, random, filesystem, sockets, CLI, HTTP, and the I/O those rest on — see [WASI 0.3 inclusion](https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/main/docs/Proposals.md#inclusion-in-wasi-03)). Native may grow **beyond** that set. Do not leave native unable to do something the wasi flavor can do.